      <div type="clause" n="1.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 1.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.3" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="150" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.2"/> ðeof on carcerne gebringe, ðæt he beo XL nihta<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.9-2"/> on carcerne, ⁊ hine mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.2"/> ðonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.11"/> lyse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.12"/> út mid CXX scll'; ⁊ ga sio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.13-2"/> mægþ him on borh<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.14"/>, ðæt he æfre geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.3" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="150" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif] mon ðeof on cwearterne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.15"/> gebringe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he beo feowertig nihta þær inne, ⁊ hine man<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.13"/> lyse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.16"/> ðænne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.9"/> ut mid hundtwelfti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.17"/> scill'; ⁊ ga seo mægð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.18"/> him on borh, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he æfre geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.3" corresp="#wit-so"><pb n="150" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif mon þeof on carcerne <hi rend="italic">ge</hi>bringe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he beo XL nihta on carcerne, ⁊ hine mon lyse þonne ut mid CXX scill'; ⁊ gá seo mægð him on borh, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he æfre geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="1.3" corresp="#wit-q"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.13-3"/><pb n="151" ed="#liebermann"/>Si fur ponatur in carcere, sit ibi XL<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.14-2"/> noctibus et inde redimatur foras<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.15-2"/> per CXX sol.; et eat cognatio eius in plegium, quod deinceps<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.16-2"/> abstineat.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="1.3" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="126" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif mon ðeof on carcerne<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#IIAs_1-3.attnote.fn.11"/> gebringe, ðæt he beo XL nihta on carcerne<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#IIAs_1-3.attnote.fn.12"/>, ⁊ hine mon ðonne<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#IIAs_1-3.attnote.fn.13"/> lyse út; mid CXX scll'; ⁊ ga sio mægþ<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_1-3.attnote.fn.1"/> him on borh, ðæt he æfre geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="151" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn ein Dieb<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.de.1"/> ins Gefängniss<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.de.2"/> gebracht wird, sei er 40 Tage im Kerker (darin <hi rend="italic">B</hi>), und dann kann er [beim König<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.de.3"/>] durch 120 Schilling<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.de.4"/> ausgelöst werden; und die Sippe gehe für ihn in Bürgschaft<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_1-3.lnote.de.5"/>, dass er immer [vom Stehlen] ablasse.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a thief is brought into prison, let him be 40 days in jail (in there, B), and then he can be redeemed [from the king] for 120 shillings; and let the kindred go surety for him that he will forever desist [from stealing].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_1-3.attnote.n.1"/><pb n="127" ed="#attenborough"/>If a thief is put in prison, he shall remain there forty days, and then he may be released on payment of 120 shillings, but his relatives shall stand as surety that he shall cease for ever after [from thieving].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="419" ed="#whitelock"/>If a thief is put into prison, he is to be in prison 40 days, and he may then be redeemed with 120 shillings; and the kindred are to stand surety for him that he will desist for ever. 1 .. And if he steals after that, they are to pay for him with his wergild, or to bring him back there.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IIAs_7">II As 7</ref>; <ref target="clause:VIAs_1-4">VI As 1.4</ref>; <ref target="clause:VIAs_12-1">VI As 12.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-sanctuary" n="140–141"><label>analogy (fails)</label> <ref target="clause:Af_42-1">Af 42.1</ref> <quote>An analogy may have been suggested by chapter 1 of Æthelstan’s ‘Grately’ code, where the circumstances concerning the handling of a thief who submits peacefully to temporary imprisonment come very close to those Alfred describes … The analogy seems to fail, however, once it is borne in mind that the person referred to in Alfred’s laws is guilty of no known offence outside of his involvement in an apparently private dispute.</quote></note>
        <note type="translator" source="#whitelock">from C.C.C.C., MS. 383</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cwearcerne <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cwearcerne Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mon <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mon Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. geänd.</hi> alyse <hi rend="italic">B;</hi> alyse <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered in the 16th cent. to alyse B; alyse Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðonne <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðonne Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-tigum <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-tigum Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mægþe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mægþe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.9-2" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Rasur hinter</hi> i</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erasure after i</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ne <hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ne written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd.</hi> alyse</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to alyse</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.13-2" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">i <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> e</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">i altered to e</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">150</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">h <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">h on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.13-3" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">151</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Rubrik</hi> Si fur ponatur in carcere <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Rubric Si fur ponatur in carcere MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.14-2" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">151</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">LX <hi rend="italic">MBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">LX MBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.15-2" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">151</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">foris <hi rend="italic">KOr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">foris KOr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.oe.16-2" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">151</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">se <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">se added by Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Auch ferner ist der strafunmündige Knabe gemeint, laut VI 12, 1 f, wo dies zitiert wird</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In what follows too the boy below the age of criminal responsibility is meant, according to VI 12, 1 f, where this is cited</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Frist 14 b. Das Gefängnis (<hi rend="italic">ebd.</hi> 6 c) dient hier neben Sicherheit auch zur Strafe; Schmid 657 b; Schreuer <hi rend="italic">Verbrechenskonk.</hi> 137</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Frist 14 b. Imprisonment (<hi rend="italic">ibid.</hi> 6 c) here serves as punishment as well as security; Schmid 657 b; Schreuer <hi rend="italic">Verbrechenskonk.</hi> 137</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dem Herrn öffentlichen Gerichts, regelmässig vertreten vom staatlichen Vogt. Diese Ergänzung bietet VI 12, 2. — Die Höhe der Bürgschaft ist danach des Knaben Wergeld. Dieser hat kein Geld, sich selbst zu lösen, weil er ein Knabe (wohl nicht, wie Schreuer meint, weil sein Vermögen dem Fiskus verfallen) ist</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">to the lord of the public court, regularly represented by the state reeve. This supplement is provided by VI 12, 2. — The amount of the surety is accordingly the boy's wergild. He has no money to redeem himself because he is a boy (probably not, as Schreuer thinks, because his property is forfeited to the fisc)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Ungehorsam 13</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Ungehorsam 13</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_1-3.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Bürgschaft 6 c; Sippe 16 h</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Bürgschaft 6 c; Sippe 16 h</seg></note>
